\ ==== slice store ====

\ slice! ( target tstart src sstart sstep slen -- target )
\ Copies slen elements: for i in 0..slen-1, target[tstart+i] = src[sstart+i*sstep].
\ Handles aliasing internally (in-place reverse and other overlapping cases).
\ Leaves target on stack.

\ Forward copy between distinct arrays
[ 0 0 0 0 0 ] 1 [ 10 20 30 ] 0 1 3 slice! . cr      \ [ 0 10 20 30 0 ]

\ Full copy at offset 0
[ 0 0 0 ] 0 [ 7 8 9 ] 0 1 3 slice! . cr             \ [ 7 8 9 ]

\ Reverse-direction read (negative step) between distinct arrays
[ 0 0 0 ] 0 [ 1 2 3 4 5 ] 4 -1 3 slice! . cr        \ [ 5 4 3 ]

\ slen = 0 is a no-op
[ 1 2 3 ] 0 [ 9 9 9 ] 0 1 0 slice! . cr             \ [ 1 2 3 ]

\ In-place reverse (source = target, sstep = -1, source starts at end of slice)
[ 1 2 3 4 5 ] 0 over 4 -1 5 slice! . cr             \ [ 5 4 3 2 1 ]

\ In-place reverse of a sub-range (positions 1..3)
[ 0 1 2 3 4 ] 1 over 3 -1 3 slice! . cr             \ [ 0 3 2 1 4 ]

\ In-place left-shift (source = target, sstart=1, sstep=1, write into 0..n-2)
[ 1 2 3 4 5 ] 0 over 1 1 4 slice! . cr              \ [ 2 3 4 5 5 ]

\ Sets via slice — source can be a set (items in sorted order)
[ 0 0 0 ] 0 [< 3 1 2 >] 0 1 3 slice! . cr             \ [ 1 2 3 ]

\ Stride >] 1 — take every other element
[ 0 0 0 ] 0 [ 1 2 3 4 5 6 ] 0 2 3 slice! . cr       \ [ 1 3 5 ]

\ Errors

\ Target out of bounds
[ 1 2 3 ] 1 [ 9 9 9 ] 0 1 3 slice!

\ Source out of bounds
[ 0 0 0 ] 0 [ 1 2 ] 0 1 3 slice!

\ Negative source index after stride
[ 0 0 0 ] 0 [ 1 2 3 ] 0 -1 3 slice!

\ Negative length
[ 0 0 0 ] 0 [ 1 2 3 ] 0 1 -1 slice!

\ Non-array source
[ 0 0 0 ] 0 42 0 1 3 slice!

\ Non-array target
"hello" 0 [ 1 2 3 ] 0 1 3 slice!

clear

\ ==== to slice ====

\ to-slice! ( v0 v1 ... vN-1 target offset N -- target )
\ Writes N stack values into target[offset..offset+N-1] in source order.
\ Top value (vN-1) goes to target[offset+N-1]. Leaves target on stack.

99 88 77 [ 0 0 0 ] 0 3 to-slice! . cr        \ [ 99 88 77 ]
99 88 77 [ 0 0 0 0 0 ] 1 3 to-slice! . cr    \ [ 0 99 88 77 0 ]
1 2 3 4 5 [ 0 0 0 0 0 ] 0 5 to-slice! . cr   \ [ 1 2 3 4 5 ]

\ count=0 is a no-op
"keep" [ 1 2 3 ] 1 0 to-slice! . cr          \ [ 1 2 3 ]
.s clear cr                                  \ [ keep ]

\ Mixed value types
"hi" :sym 42 [ 0 0 0 ] 0 3 to-slice! . cr    \ [ hi :sym 42 ]

\ Errors
[ 0 0 0 ] 5 3 to-slice!
[ 0 0 0 ] 0 -1 to-slice!
99 88 77 42 0 3 to-slice!
1 2 [ 0 0 0 0 0 ] 0 5 to-slice!

clear

\ ==== reverse slice ====

\ In-place reversal through the general strided slice!: source and target the
\ same array, step -1, ends aligned ( arr offset n -- arr ).

: rev! | arr off n |
  arr off  arr off n f+ f1-  -1 n slice! ;

variable nums

[ 1 2 3 4 5 ] to nums   nums 0 5 rev! drop   nums . cr   \ [ 5 4 3 2 1 ]
[ 1 2 3 4 5 ] to nums   nums 0 3 rev! drop   nums . cr   \ [ 3 2 1 4 5 ]
[ 1 2 3 4 5 ] to nums   nums 1 3 rev! drop   nums . cr   \ [ 1 4 3 2 5 ]
[ 1 2 3 4 5 ] to nums   nums 2 1 rev! drop   nums . cr   \ single element, unchanged
[ 1 2 3 4 5 ] to nums   nums 2 0 rev! drop   nums . cr   \ empty slice, unchanged
[ 9 ] to nums   nums 0 1 rev! drop   nums . cr           \ [ 9 ]

\ it leaves the array, so it chains
[ 1 2 3 4 5 ] 0 5 rev! . cr                     \ [ 5 4 3 2 1 ]

\ errors
[ 1 2 3 ] 0 5 rev!     \ slice past the end
[ 1 2 3 ] 2 2 rev!     \ offset + n past the end
[ 1 2 3 ] -1 2 rev!    \ negative offset
[ 1 2 3 ] 0 -1 rev!    \ negative count
5 0 1 rev!             \ not an array

clear
